  experimentTitle: EXPERIMENT TITLE
  experimentSteps:
  - 'Step 1: Select the frequency of the source tuning fork'
  - 'Step 2: Strike the source tuning fork'
  - Resonance occurred! Both tuning forks have the same natural frequency
  - No resonance occurred because the frequencies do not match
  - "Experiment Completed! \u2713\r\n\r\nWhy did this happen?\r\nResonance occurs
    when the driving frequency matches an object's natural frequency. At 440 Hz,
    energy transfers efficiently to the second tuning fork, causing it to vibrate.
    At 512 Hz, the frequencies do not match, so resonance does not occur."
